WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.418
Database design can be discussed at three

00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:06.664
levels The conceptual level is the business

00:00:06.677 --> 00:00:10.299
view We identify major subjects and high-level

00:00:10.312 --> 00:00:15.471
relationships without worrying about PostgreSQL
syntax The

00:00:15.498 --> 00:00:17.853
logical level turns that business view into

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:21.895
a relational blueprint We decide tables attributes

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.987
primary keys foreign keys cardinality optionality
and

00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:30.429
normalization The physical level is the actual

00:00:30.442 --> 00:00:34.840
database implementation Here we choose PostgreSQL
data

00:00:34.866 --> 00:00:38.616
types indexes storage decisions and deployment
details

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.788
Keeping these levels separate is helpful because

00:00:42.814 --> 00:00:44.827
business meaning should not depend on one

00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:49.958
technical implementation For example the logical
idea

00:00:49.984 --> 00:00:51.852
that an appointment belongs to a patient

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:54.247
remains valid even if the physical indexing

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.707
strategy changes later
